--- RULE FILE = lvs.ctrl

// lvs.ctrl -- Calibre LVS control file for the clean-slate layout (task 066)
// NEW FILE: LVS has never been run on this project (handoff 18.24: "first time"). There is no old file to copy.
// Every statement below is VERIFY until the first run; the README lists what to read in the log and the report.
// Written from the DRC/antenna control files that worked (drc.ctrl, ant.ctrl) plus standard SVRF specification statements.
// Run folder: pnr_icc2/calibre/run1/lvs/ (unpu_top.sp is written there by v2lvs, see README step 7)
//
// VERIFY: the deck may need its own #define switches (the DRC deck refused to run without 4M1L/BLOCK/3V, handoff 18.24).
// The README step "read the LVS deck switches" prints the deck's #ifdef/#ifndef/#define lines; add the switches it demands, none are guessed here except 4M1L.
#define 4M1L
// FILTER_DWN2PSUB (task 073, user approved 2026-11-09). Reason: the layout has one extra device D(DWN2PSUB), the N-well to P-substrate diode (76 parallel diodes reduced to 1) of the N-well of the
// feedth* filler cells. It is a parasitic junction with no schematic equivalent, and the kit CDL defines feedth, feedth3, feedth9 as EMPTY subcircuits, so the source cannot carry it.
// The deck provides this switch for it (LVS FILTER D(dwn2psub) OPEN, deck lines 4016 to 4018). With it nets and instances match 100 percent. BLOCK_DWN2PSUB (extraction off) is NOT used.
#define FILTER_DWN2PSUB
// VERIFY: same name as in drc.ctrl; if the layout and source names of the top cell differ, set LAYOUT PRIMARY from the README step "find the GDS top cell name"
// 082: RELATIVE on purpose (VERIFY V18: Calibre resolves LAYOUT PATH from the folder it is started in, like SOURCE PATH / MASK SVDB DIRECTORY). Start it from <RUN_DIR>/pnr_icc2/calibre/run1/lvs/ (README step 2): ../../../outputs is then THIS clone's pnr_icc2/outputs, never another clone's.
LAYOUT PATH "../../../outputs/unpu_top_routed.gds"
LAYOUT PRIMARY "unpu_top"
LAYOUT SYSTEM GDSII
// source = SPICE written by v2lvs from unpu_top_pnr_pg.v (README step 7); the top subckt is named after the Verilog top module (VERIFY with grep -i subckt)
SOURCE PATH "unpu_top.sp"
SOURCE PRIMARY "unpu_top"
SOURCE SYSTEM SPICE
// VERIFY: the deck may already define the report and the SVDB; if Calibre reports a duplicate or conflicting statement, remove the statement here (do not edit the deck)
LVS REPORT "unpu_top.lvs.rpt"
MASK SVDB DIRECTORY "svdb"
// Power and ground names: NOT set here (VERIFY: the deck normally has LVS POWER NAME / LVS GROUND NAME; grep for them in the README step).
// If the report says the supply nets are not recognised, add: LVS POWER NAME "VDD" and LVS GROUND NAME "VSS"
INCLUDE "/storage/EE5239G1/aagams_workspace/calibre_run/scr/LVS_TS18SL_SCL_CALIBRE"


